{% extends 'dashboard/help/_topic.html.twig' %}
{% block content %}
<p>A client may only send with a From address at a <strong>sending domain</strong> it has proven to control, and in production only once the domain also has an active DKIM key.</p>
<ol>
<li>The domain is added (client dashboard or <code>smarthost:domain:add</code>); catto-mail shows a TXT record: <code>_smarthost-verification.&lt;domain&gt;</code> with a random token.</li>
<li>The record is created at the domain's DNS; catto-mail checks it (<code>smarthost:domain:verify</code>, or the dashboard) and marks the domain verified.</li>
<li>A DKIM key is generated, published and activated (System setup › DKIM).</li>
<li>Recommended: a DMARC record at the domain.</li>
</ol>
<p>The domain can belong to the client organisation; its DNS records then have to be created by them.</p>
{% endblock %}
